5:["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"One interface, 8 providers"}]," — Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, AWS Bedrock, Groq, Mistral, Azure OpenAI, and Ollama, all implementing the same ",["$","code",null,{"children":"Provider"}]," contract."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"A real agent runtime"}]," —"," ",["$","code",null,{"children":"defineAgent()"}],", multi-agent handoffs with loop prevention, and a run loop that owns tool execution itself so behavior doesn't vary by provider."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Guardrails and approval"}]," — PII redaction, prompt-injection blocking, budget caps, schema validation on output, and a fail-closed approval gate for risky tools."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Typed tools"}]," — ",["$","code",null,{"children":"defineTool()"}]," infers argument types from a zod or valibot schema, and validates incoming args before your code runs."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Sessions, RAG, MCP, and graph memory"}]," — in-memory, file, Redis, or SQLite session persistence; a retrieval pipeline for grounding agents in your documents; a client for any MCP server; and a Neo4j-backed per-user knowledge graph for long-term memory that survives across sessions."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Production concerns, not afterthoughts"}]," — retries, fallback chains, timeouts, concurrency/rate limiting, checkpoint resume, and full run tracing with an OpenTelemetry export and a local HTML trace viewer."]}]]}]
